{
  "format": 1,
  "conventions": {
    "files": "Each prop is one object in its own SVG, drawn at its own size in this folder.",
    "size": "Props are drawn for a 1920 by 1080 movie at about real size beside the starter characters (about 265 px to the metre at the floor, as the starter scenes are); small things such as food are drawn a little larger so they read. In a movie of another size a prop is scaled as a starter scene would be, and never larger than the frame.",
    "base": "base is the y in the SVG's own pixels where the prop stands: the centre line of the soft contact shadow at its bottom. A prop with a base stands on the movie's floor guide; a prop without one (it flies or is held) is placed in the middle of the frame.",
    "styles": "flat: solid shapes, no outlines. outline: a hand-drawn ink line over paper and soft colours. stick: thick round lines and few fills.",
    "elements": "Only path, rect, circle and ellipse with solid fills (fill-opacity for soft shadows), strokes and no groups. No text, gradients, filters, masks, patterns, images or CSS, so each shape stays a vector shape in the movie.",
    "license": "Original artwork made for this project and covered by the repository's own license."
  },
